extraction_notes: |
  - Triax and the NGR, printed 197-199, under the heading *Optional Player
    Characters*. One of five gargoyle R.C.C.s in this book.
  - THIS ENTRY AND THE GURGOYLE''S ARE ONE ENTRY IN THE BOOK AND TWO ROWS HERE.
    Printed 198 heads them together and then states them separately at every
    point that matters: two attribute lines, two M.D.C. formulas, two horror
    factors, two running speeds, two leap distances, and a skills list that
    diverges by species - escape artist is gurgoyle-only, and swim is +10% for
    the gurgoyle and MINUS 10% for the gargoyle. One row could not hold both
    without discarding half of each. The survey called this split before the
    import and it is why this book has twenty-one playable classes from twenty
    entries.
  - AN ABSENT LADDER ON PRINTED 224 IS NOT A VERDICT HERE. None of the five
    gargoyle R.C.C.s carries one, and each states outright that player
    characters use another class''s table - this one the psi-stalker''s, which
    resolves in this catalog as `psi-stalker` and `wild-psi-stalker`. That is
    affirmative language about playability, and the section heading on printed
    197 calls them optional player characters. Nothing is stored: a Rifts class
    carries no `xp_table` here.
  - `Language: Gargoyle` IS A NEW CATALOG ROW, created by this batch. It is one
    of the two new skills the survey''s diff found on printed 155, the other
    being Language: Brodkil, which no class in this book grants.
  - RELATED AND SECONDARY SKILLS NORMALLY COME FROM THE O.C.C. AND THIS R.C.C.
    GRANTS SECONDARY SKILLS ANYWAY, because the book does: these are optional
    player characters played AS the race, with no occupation, so the R.C.C.''s
    own list is all they get. It grants no O.C.C. Related Skills and that
    absence is correct.
  - THE SECONDARY-SKILL EXCLUSION IS NOT ENFORCED. The book allows six from any
    category except electrical, mechanical, medical and science.
    `secondary_skills` takes a count and a schedule; a category restriction on
    it is not a shape the block has, and a category `bonus` there is a parse
    error by design. The exclusion is in the block''s note, where the player
    sees it at the pick.
  - THE FLYING SPEED IS NOT STORED. Spd is one attribute and it holds the
    running speed of 5D6; the flying speed of 2D4x10+10 is in the natural
    abilities and the restrictions. Same for the +4 to dodge while in flight,
    which is conditional and therefore prose by rule - the +2 dodge that
    applies always is stored.
  - `psionics.type` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. The entry names eight powers and
    says the creature is "equal to a 6th level psychic", which is a power level
    rather than one of the minor/major/master tiers, and it states no psionic
    save target of its own. Writing a tier here would invent one; the +1 to
    save vs psionic attacks the entry DOES print is stored as a save bonus.
